  "summary": "I added a 'Tour' button in a bar directly below the canvas, in the page flow. I only ran `typecheck`, which passes; I haven't run the tour in a browser.\n\n- **Tour:** clicking it focuses Mercury, then each planet outwards at 3 s per planet. Each step includes the 1.5 s camera move, and the info panel shows throughout. After Neptune it returns to the overview and the label goes back to 'Tour'.\n- **While touring:** the button reads 'Stop tour'. Clicking it ends the tour and eases back to the overview.\n- **State:** `window.__TASK_STATE__` now has a read-only `touring` boolean.\n- **Cancelling:** any manual focus action also cancels a running tour. That covers clicking a planet or empty space, pressing Escape, and calling `__focusPlanet` or `__unfocus`. A manual planet click leaves the camera focused on that planet. This was my choice, not something you asked for.\n- **Timing:** the tour's timing uses real time, so pausing the orbits doesn't stall it.\n\nAll changes are in `src/main.ts`."
